From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 21:15:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] soc/intel/cannonlake: Clear the watchdog's reset status once
 it is logged

Romstage logs that the last reset came from the firmware watchdog when
ICCSURV_STS or NO_ICCSURV_STS of OC_WDT_CTL is set, and every write of
the common code now leaves those bits as they are, so that they are not
lost before the log. Nothing cleared them after it: one reset by the
watchdog would be reported at every boot that follows, for as long as
the register keeps the bits. The Lynx Point twin of this code clears
them right after its log.

Add oc_wdt_clear_reset_status() and call it after the log, which now
has the register too, as on Lynx Point.

The path is still untested on a machine: no reset by the watchdog was
ever provoked on the ThinkCentre M920x.

TEST=Build of the ThinkCentre M920x.
---
 src/soc/intel/cannonlake/firmware_watchdog.c         |  8 ++++++--
 .../intel/common/block/include/intelblocks/oc_wdt.h  |  1 +
 src/soc/intel/common/block/oc_wdt/oc_wdt.c           | 12 +++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/firmware_watchdog.c b/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/firmware_watchdog.c
index 21879fac..df0a3db2 100644
--- a/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/firmware_watchdog.c
+++ b/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/firmware_watchdog.c
@@ -36,8 +36,12 @@ void firmware_watchdog_romstage(bool s3wake)
 {
 	const unsigned int t = firmware_watchdog_timeout();
 
-	if (oc_wdt_caused_reset())
-		printk(BIOS_WARNING, "Firmware watchdog: the last reset came from the watchdog\n");
+	if (oc_wdt_caused_reset()) {
+		printk(BIOS_WARNING, "Firmware watchdog: the last reset came from the watchdog "
+		       "(OC_WDT_CTL 0x%08x)\n", oc_wdt_read());
+		/* Clear the status, so that the next boot does not report it again */
+		oc_wdt_clear_reset_status();
+	}
 
 	if (t && !s3wake) {
 		oc_wdt_arm(t);
diff --git a/src/soc/intel/common/block/include/intelblocks/oc_wdt.h b/src/soc/intel/common/block/include/intelblocks/oc_wdt.h
index 7b40869d..dd27255e 100644
--- a/src/soc/intel/common/block/include/intelblocks/oc_wdt.h
+++ b/src/soc/intel/common/block/include/intelblocks/oc_wdt.h
@@ -20,5 +20,6 @@ void oc_wdt_arm(unsigned int timeout);
 void oc_wdt_stop(void);
 uint32_t oc_wdt_read(void);
 bool oc_wdt_caused_reset(void);
+void oc_wdt_clear_reset_status(void);
 
 #endif
diff --git a/src/soc/intel/common/block/oc_wdt/oc_wdt.c b/src/soc/intel/common/block/oc_wdt/oc_wdt.c
index 891bf8fc..f870f63d 100644
--- a/src/soc/intel/common/block/oc_wdt/oc_wdt.c
+++ b/src/soc/intel/common/block/oc_wdt/oc_wdt.c
@@ -115,12 +115,22 @@ uint32_t oc_wdt_read(void)
 	return inl(PCH_OC_WDT_CTL);
 }
 
-/* Whether the last reset came from the watchdog, read before any write clears it */
+/* Whether the last reset came from the watchdog, until the status is cleared */
 bool oc_wdt_caused_reset(void)
 {
 	return inl(PCH_OC_WDT_CTL) & PCH_OC_WDT_CTL_STS_MASK;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Clear the status of a reset by the watchdog (write-1-to-clear), once it is
+ * logged: every other write here leaves it as it is, so the boots that follow
+ * would report the same reset again.
+ */
+void oc_wdt_clear_reset_status(void)
+{
+	outl(inl(PCH_OC_WDT_CTL) & ~PCH_OC_WDT_CTL_RLD, PCH_OC_WDT_CTL);
+}
+
 /* Returns currently programmed OC watchdog timeout in seconds */
 unsigned int oc_wdt_get_current_timeout(void)
 {
-- 
